  }),
  faqSchema({
    questions: [
      { question: "If Ethernet works through my USB-C hub, doesn't that mean the USB-C port supports everything?", answer: "No. Ethernet uses USB data. HDMI on many hubs depends on a separate DisplayPort Alt Mode path from the host. One can work while the other is unavailable." },
      { question: "Can a charge-only USB-C port still run hub Ethernet?", answer: "A USB-C port that supports USB data can run an Ethernet adapter even if it does not expose a display signal. Charging support is a separate capability again." },
